course: dictionary
lesson: 10588
title: Underline
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To underline a word is to draw a straight line under it, usually with a ruler or pencil. Teachers ask you to do this to show what matters most. «Underlining the key words in a question helps you see exactly what is asked.»
explain: Underline is also used to mean show that something is important. «The accident underlines the need for helmets» means the accident shows clearly why helmets matter. Here the word is a verb, an action, but it does not mean drawing a line.
explain: Underline changes its form: underline, underlines, underlined, underlining. Pick the one that fits the time. «She underlined the date» is about the past. «He is underlining the verbs» is happening now. Read the sentence to choose the right form.
fact: Underline is a verb: underline, underlines, underlined, underlining.
fact: An underline is also a noun: it is the line you draw under a word.
fact: To underline is to draw a line under a word or words to show they are important or to mark a title.
fact: «Underline the title and the date» means draw a line under those two things.
fact: To underline something can also mean to show or stress that it is important, as in «the accident underlines the need for helmets».
exercise: «Underlining the key words in a question helps you see exactly what is asked.» What does underlining do here? | It answers the question for you | It rubs out the words | It makes the question longer | *It shows the most important words
exercise: Mrs Patel says, «Underline the verbs in this sentence.» What should you do? | *Draw a line under each verb | Circle every noun only | Rub out every verb | Write the verbs in capital letters
exercise: «Yesterday Sam ___ the title with a ruler.» Which word fits the gap? | *underlined | underlines | underlining | underline
test: «The accident underlines the need for helmets.» What does underlines mean here? | It draws a line on the road | It hides the need for helmets | It forgets about helmets | *It shows clearly that something is important
test: In «Draw an underline beneath the date», what is an underline? | *The line you draw under a word | A word that means very old | The date itself | A kind of pencil
exam: «First the team reads the case together, underlines the key facts and lists the stakeholders.» What does underlines mean here? | Throws the facts away | Hides the facts from others | Reads the facts out loud | *Marks the key facts so they stand out
